### Task Management API — Auth flows
# Pick an environment first: VS Code REST Client status-bar env picker, or Rider's env dropdown.
# Requests below use variables from http-client.env.json (local / docker).

@contentType = {{contentType}}

### Health check (no auth)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Register a brand-new user (self-registration always yields the Developer role)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "newuser@example.com",
  "password": "Sup3rSecret!",
  "firstName": "New",
  "lastName": "User"
}

### Log in as the seeded admin — captures tokens for every request below
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

###
@accessToken = {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
@refreshToken = {{login.response.body.$.refreshToken}}

### Log in as other seeded roles (swap the vars to test RBAC)
# @name loginManager
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "{{managerEmail}}",
  "password": "{{managerPassword}}"
}

### Smoke a protected endpoint with the captured token
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks?pageSize=1
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Refresh the token pair
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "accessToken": "{{accessToken}}",
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

### Change password (invalidates the current refresh token)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/change-password
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "currentPassword": "{{adminPassword}}",
  "newPassword": "Admin@1234"
}

### Log out (revokes the refresh token)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
